  "notes": "\"Boom-bap drums under R&B hooks\" is the whole entry, and the parameter that carries it is the mix rather than the pattern: `percs` runs four lanes with `gainOffsetDb` -3, the hats split evenly between 8ths and 16ths, and `fillDensity` sits at 0.56 — the club top-end the research contrasts against the 90s norm. Harmony is the pop half: I–V–vi–IV as the primary family with i–VI–VII behind it. The synth-or-guitar riff answering the sung hook is the countermelody, so it sits an octave *above* the lead at `densityRatio` 0.52 with `answer_lick` weighted 4. ⚠ `medium`, and the research names the inferred parameter itself: \"parameters largely producer-inherited\". The kick grammar, ghost placement and swing amount here are the early-2000s NY radio norm, not a measurement of Fabolous records; the I–IV–V and i–iv families at weight 2 are reductions of the two researched families.",
